julia: FYI I ran into three related doc issues while prepping the migration guide: streaming + retries examples are inconsistent across languages, pagination link on the migration page points to an old header, and our Go snippet failed the docs CI. Can someone own a compact polyglot cookbook we can reference?

omar: I can. prefer one doc with language tabs so it's easier to keep synced. will keep examples tiny.

ryan: CI note: docs-snippet-check flagged the Go example with a data race when buffering responses. paste of the failing line: `WARNING: goroutine leak: stream reader used concurrently` — swapping to channel-per-stream fixed it locally.

lee: +1 one page. requirement: show (1) streaming with resume token persistence, (2) idempotent retry using resume_token, (3) top-level pagination cursor usage. tiny samples, no heavy wrappers.

omar: draft TS snippet (very small):

```ts
// streaming + resume + paginate (compact)
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'
const client = new Redwood.Client()

// first request
let cursor_id = null
for await (const tok of client.stream('gpt-xx', { prompt: '...', maxTokens: 512 })) {
  if (tok.type === 'resume') {
    cursor_id = tok.token // persist
  }
  process.stdout.write(tok.delta || '')
}

// retry using saved token
await client.stream('gpt-xx', { resumeToken: cursor_id })

// pagination example (top-level fetch)
const batch_size = 50
let page = await client.list('items', { limit: batch_size })
while (page.items.length) {
  // process
  if (!page.next_cursor) break
  page = await client.list('items', { cursor: page.next_cursor, limit: batch_size })
}
```

omar: will add Py/Go analogs mirroring the same var names: `cursor_id`, `resume_token`, `batch_size`.

tara: please include a short callout: resume tokens are best-effort, may expire (TTL varies), and do not guarantee exactly-once semantics. also mention batching vs realtime tradeoffs (cost/latency).

ryan: here's the minimal Go fix I used (channels + context):

```go
// minimal go streaming + resume
ctx := context.Background()
client := redwood.NewClient()

var resume_token string
ch := make(chan string)

go func() {
  defer close(ch)
  stream := client.Stream(ctx, "gpt-xx", redwood.StreamOpts{MaxTokens:512})
  for item := range stream.Chunks() {
    if item.Type == redwood.ResumeChunk {
      resume_token = item.Token // persist safely (single goroutine)
    }
    ch <- item.Text
  }
}()

for txt := range ch {
  fmt.Print(txt)
}

// retry
if resume_token != "" {
  client.Stream(ctx, "gpt-xx", redwood.StreamOpts{ResumeToken:resume_token})
}
```

ryan: that removes the shared buffer and aligns with the CI validator. i'll open a small fix PR for the failing snippet if omar wants to coordinate.

omar: please do. plan: branch `docs/sdks/mini-cookbook-resume-retry-cursor`, add page with three language tabs, update migration guide anchor links, and add a one-line note on resume semantics. will include `make docs-validate-snippets` in the PR description. target: submit tomorrow morning.

